      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings released: EPS: ₹7.20 (vs ₹6.84 in FY 2025)",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹7.20 (up from ₹6.84 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹27.5b (down 1.5% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹1.79b (up 5.2% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 6.5% (up from 6.1% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by lower expenses. Revenue is forecast to grow 6.8% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 12% growth forecast for the Luxury industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 1% per year but the company’s share price has fallen by 27% per year, which means it is performing significantly worse than earnings.",
